---
import { url } from "../../lib/url";
---

<section id="small" class="section wrap" aria-labelledby="small-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">01 / A small beginning</p>
            <h2 id="small-title">What would be useful <em>right now?</em></h2>
          </div>
          <p>No need to name your state.<br />Just choose a direction.</p>
        </div>
        <div id="picker">
          <fieldset class="choices" hidden>
            <legend class="sr-only">Choose a kind of beginning</legend>
            <label
              ><input
                type="radio"
                name="beginning"
                value="outside"
                checked
              /><span class="choice"
                ><span class="choice-icon" aria-hidden="true">▧</span
                ><strong>Something outside me</strong
                ><span>Start with the room.</span></span
              ></label
            >
            <label
              ><input type="radio" name="beginning" value="movement" /><span
                class="choice"
                ><span class="choice-icon" aria-hidden="true">〰</span
                ><strong>A little movement</strong
                ><span>There’s no need to sit still.</span></span
              ></label
            >
            <label
              ><input type="radio" name="beginning" value="read" /><span
                class="choice"
                ><span class="choice-icon" aria-hidden="true">Aa</span
                ><strong>Help me understand</strong
                ><span>Reading is a beginning, too.</span></span
              ></label
            >
            <label
              ><input type="radio" name="beginning" value="support" /><span
                class="choice"
                ><span class="choice-icon" aria-hidden="true">↗</span
                ><strong>A bit of support</strong
                ><span>You can bring someone in.</span></span
              ></label
            >
          </fieldset>
          <p id="choice-status" class="sr-only" role="status"></p>
          <div class="invitation" data-panel="outside">
            <div class="invitation-number" aria-hidden="true">a.</div>
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">An invitation · a few moments</p>
              <h3>Let an ordinary thing be ordinary.</h3>
              <p>
                If you like, find an object near you: a cup, a window, a fold in
                a blanket. Notice one shape or color. You don’t need to feel
                anything in particular.
              </p>
              <p class="gentle-note">
                Looking around doesn’t suit everyone. You can skip this, move,
                or just read.
              </p>
              <div class="invitation-actions">
                <button class="button dark done" hidden>
                  That’s enough for now
                  <span aria-hidden="true">✓</span></button
                ><a
                  class="text-link"
                  href={url("practices/orienting/")}
                  >More about orienting →</a
                >
              </div>
            </div>
            <svg
              class="cup decoration"
              viewBox="0 0 150 150"
              aria-hidden="true"
            >
              <ellipse cx="72" cy="120" rx="57" ry="9" fill="#bac4a4" />
              <path
                d="M32 40h73v61q-2 25-37 25-35 0-36-25Z"
                fill="#f7f0e4"
                stroke="#718369"
                stroke-width="2"
              />
              <path
                d="M106 50q46-7 22 46-6 7-20 4"
                fill="none"
                stroke="#718369"
                stroke-width="6"
              />
              <path d="M43 54h50" stroke="#a3ae8f" stroke-width="2" />
              <path
                d="m61 86 5 3m16-3-5 3"
                stroke="#53644e"
                stroke-width="3"
                stroke-linecap="round"
              />
            </svg>
          </div>
          <div class="invitation" data-panel="movement">
            <div class="invitation-number" aria-hidden="true">b.</div>
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">An invitation · your choice of pace</p>
              <h3>Change one small thing.</h3>
              <p>
                If moving is comfortable for you, try shifting your position or
                moving a hand in a way you already know feels okay. Small is
                plenty. There’s no particular sensation to find.
              </p>
              <p class="gentle-note">
                Stay within a comfortable range. Skip anything painful,
                dizzying, or unwelcome.
              </p>
              <div class="invitation-actions">
                <button class="button dark done" hidden>
                  That’s enough for now
                  <span aria-hidden="true">✓</span></button
                ><a class="text-link" href="#understand">I’d rather read →</a>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="invitation" data-panel="read">
            <div class="invitation-number" aria-hidden="true">c.</div>
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">No exercise needed</p>
              <h3>You can start with a little context.</h3>
              <p>
                The internet has a lot of vocabulary for how we feel. You don’t
                need to learn it all before you begin. Start with the three
                ideas below, or take the introductory tour.
              </p>
              <div class="invitation-actions">
                <a class="button dark" href="#understand"
                  >Read three useful ideas ↓</a
                ><a
                  class="text-link"
                  href={url("start/")}
                  >Visit the introductory tour ↗</a
                ><button class="text-link done" hidden>Done for now</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="invitation" data-panel="support">
            <div class="invitation-number" aria-hidden="true">d.</div>
            <div>
              <p class="eyebrow">You can bring someone in</p>
              <h3>Support belongs in the picture.</h3>
              <p>
                A trusted person, an accommodating environment, or a qualified
                clinician may be more useful than another exercise. If symptoms
                are persistent or disrupting daily life, a clinician can help
                you explore what’s going on.
              </p>
              <p class="gentle-note">
                For people exploring PTSD care, this public guide explains
                treatment options. This website provides education, not
                assessment or treatment.
              </p>
              <div class="invitation-actions">
                <a
                  class="button dark"
                  href="https://www.ptsd.va.gov/apps/decisionaid/"
                  >Explore PTSD care options ↗</a
                ><button class="text-link done" hidden>Done for now</button>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="ending" id="ending" hidden>
          <span aria-hidden="true">✳</span>
          <h3 id="ending-title" tabindex="-1">That can be enough.</h3>
          <p>
            No next step required. You can close this page, carry on with your
            day, or come back when you like.
          </p>
          <button class="text-link" id="restart">
            Choose another beginning ↺
          </button>
        </div>
        <p class="section-footnote">
          These are optional everyday experiments, not tests or trauma
          treatment. Nothing you select is saved.
        </p>
      </section>
